{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"af8f29d213b6","type":"group","x":-30,"y":-60,"width":1280,"height":490,"label":"Incident Overview","color":"1"},
		{"id":"88743a2d4257","type":"group","x":1380,"y":-60,"width":1280,"height":490,"label":"Affected Entities","color":"5"},
		{"id":"16995422fa0d","type":"group","x":-30,"y":490,"width":400,"height":1520,"label":"Phase 1 - Initial execution","color":"6"},
		{"id":"f24700833143","type":"group","x":430,"y":490,"width":400,"height":1520,"label":"Phase 2 - Credential discovery","color":"6"},
		{"id":"41e84de90de1","type":"group","x":890,"y":490,"width":400,"height":1520,"label":"Phase 3 - Domain reconnaissance","color":"6"},
		{"id":"829692412ecf","type":"group","x":1350,"y":490,"width":400,"height":1520,"label":"Phase 4 - Lateral movement","color":"6"},
		{"id":"70449539875c","type":"group","x":1810,"y":490,"width":400,"height":1520,"label":"Phase 5 - Data staging","color":"6"},
		{"id":"2a09bb8a142b","type":"group","x":2270,"y":490,"width":400,"height":1520,"label":"Phase 6 - Outbound connection","color":"6"},
		{"id":"516e1f641781","type":"group","x":-30,"y":2090,"width":760,"height":710,"label":"Hypotheses (analytical, not established fact)","color":"2"},
		{"id":"cdabe3ef03c5","type":"group","x":830,"y":2090,"width":760,"height":710,"label":"Timestamp and Correlation Issues","color":"3"},
		{"id":"54396620620a","type":"group","x":1730,"y":2090,"width":760,"height":710,"label":"Final Assessment","color":"1"},
		{"id":"c75e06854868","type":"group","x":970,"y":2880,"width":1520,"height":500,"label":"Recommended Investigation and Response","color":"2"},
		{"id":"f93a7e1ea140","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":400,"height":160,"text":"# Quiet as the Grave\nSuspected intrusion, lateral movement and data exfiltration\n**Incident date:** Oct 25, 2026","color":"1"},
		{"id":"a30d3b10aeff","type":"text","x":460,"y":0,"width":320,"height":120,"text":"**Severity:** High / Critical\n**Assessment:** True Positive","color":"1"},
		{"id":"e7e28b66d1f9","type":"text","x":840,"y":0,"width":380,"height":160,"text":"**Limitation:** the evidence does not prove credential theft, successful archive transfer, or how the script reached the second host","color":"3"},
		{"id":"c89d506b530d","type":"text","x":0,"y":280,"width":1220,"height":120,"text":"Word document spawns hidden PowerShell that downloads `svchost_update.ps1`, then credential discovery and domain recon, a remote SYSTEM service on THM-SREYES, a 7-Zip archive of the NeuralNexus build, and an outbound connection to `45.147.230.131:8067`."},
		{"id":"92a7b5e1303a","type":"text","x":1410,"y":0,"width":260,"height":160,"text":"**THM-MSMITH**\n`10.60.10.22`\nInitial suspected compromised host"},
		{"id":"09b088d66d78","type":"text","x":1730,"y":0,"width":260,"height":160,"text":"**THM-SREYES**\n`10.60.10.20`\nTarget of remote service and archive creation"},
		{"id":"d86e8e9986f5","type":"text","x":2050,"y":10,"width":260,"height":140,"text":"**TRYHATME\\m.smith**\nInitial execution and recon user"},
		{"id":"1352812aab0b","type":"text","x":2370,"y":0,"width":260,"height":160,"text":"**TRYHATME\\svc-mktshare**\nRegistered the remote service"},
		{"id":"e808b637493f","type":"text","x":1410,"y":220,"width":260,"height":140,"text":"**NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM**\nContext of payload and archive processes"},
		{"id":"d25c9f183c74","type":"text","x":1730,"y":220,"width":260,"height":140,"text":"**paylink-cdn.thm:8067**\nHost embedded in the initial download command"},
		{"id":"733aef888d92","type":"text","x":2050,"y":210,"width":260,"height":160,"text":"**45.147.230.131:8067**\nSuspicious external destination seen on both hosts","color":"1"},
		{"id":"75a5e314e7a3","type":"text","x":2370,"y":210,"width":260,"height":160,"text":"**104.18.32.47:443**\nExternal destination needing independent investigation","color":"3"},
		{"id":"ad959a2d280f","type":"text","x":0,"y":550,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"## Phase 1\nInitial execution and payload retrieval\n`05:43:10-05:43:12`","color":"6"},
		{"id":"015331d345e5","type":"text","x":0,"y":760,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**POC 1 - Word process**\n`WINWORD.EXE` (PID 6184) opened `Q3_PressKit_Feedback.docm` at 05:43:10.083","color":"5"},
		{"id":"b47e693e97b5","type":"text","x":0,"y":970,"width":340,"height":260,"text":"**POC 2 - Hidden PowerShell**\nChild of Word: `powershell.exe -NoP -W Hidden -Enc <Base64>`\nDecoded: downloads `http://paylink-cdn.thm:8067/svchost_update.ps1` to `%TEMP%` and runs it with execution policy bypass","color":"5"},
		{"id":"ebc2c31cd1f9","type":"text","x":0,"y":1280,"width":340,"height":200,"text":"**Assessment**\nStrong evidence of document-associated script execution. The exact trigger (e.g. macro) is not proven."},
		{"id":"c54715183164","type":"text","x":0,"y":1530,"width":340,"height":200,"text":"**Timestamp conflict**\nA network event to `45.147.230.131:8067` at 05:42:16 predates the Word event. Reconcile against raw logs.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"7d778aacccf2","type":"text","x":460,"y":550,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"## Phase 2\nCredential discovery\n`about 05:42-05:43 (ordering needs validation)`","color":"6"},
		{"id":"083615f2fcd8","type":"text","x":460,"y":760,"width":340,"height":260,"text":"**POC 3 - VaultCmd**\n`VaultCmd.exe /listcreds:Windows Credentials`\nParent: PowerShell running `svchost_update.ps1` as `m.smith`\nProcess Access: PowerShell to VaultCmd, `GrantedAccess=0x1FFFFF`","color":"5"},
		{"id":"08eccdd1b867","type":"text","x":460,"y":1070,"width":340,"height":140,"text":"**Assessment**\nConsistent with attempted discovery of stored Windows credentials."},
		{"id":"c69fa3d67435","type":"text","x":460,"y":1260,"width":340,"height":200,"text":"**Unconfirmed**\nListing credentials does not prove secrets were extracted. The access mask alone does not prove theft.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"9b595e07e7f8","type":"text","x":920,"y":550,"width":340,"height":140,"text":"## Phase 3\nDomain reconnaissance\n`05:48:16`","color":"6"},
		{"id":"38ac3eb12c1f","type":"text","x":920,"y":740,"width":340,"height":260,"text":"**POC 4 - Process creation**\nFrom hidden PowerShell:\n`net.exe user /domain`\n`net.exe group \"Domain Admins\" /domain`\n`nltest.exe /dclist:tryhatmestudios.thm`","color":"5"},
		{"id":"e4e494ff9ca8","type":"text","x":920,"y":1050,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**Assessment**\nConsistent with mapping Active Directory after gaining code execution."},
		{"id":"3d1c836e39dc","type":"text","x":920,"y":1260,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**Unconfirmed**\nCommand output was not supplied, so no specific users or DCs should be asserted.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"ce6a476ac817","type":"text","x":1380,"y":550,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"## Phase 4\nLateral movement toward THM-SREYES\n`05:49:16-05:53:41`","color":"6"},
		{"id":"40d720d798a3","type":"text","x":1380,"y":760,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**POC 5 - Admin share attempt**\n`net.exe use \\\\THM-SREYES\\C$`\nAn access attempt; success is not proven.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"10e740ee5292","type":"text","x":1380,"y":970,"width":340,"height":360,"text":"**POC 6 - Remote service (EID 4697)**\n05:49:47 `SvcUpdate` registered on THM-SREYES by `svc-mktshare` (logon ID `0x24F6572`)\nRuns as LocalSystem, manual start:\n`cmd.exe /c start /b powershell.exe -NoP -NonI -W Hidden -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\\Windows\\Temp\\svchost_update.ps1`","color":"1"},
		{"id":"6b35bb1bdada","type":"text","x":1380,"y":1380,"width":340,"height":140,"text":"**POC 7 - Service start**\n05:53:41 `sc.exe \\\\THM-SREYES start SvcUpdate`","color":"5"},
		{"id":"a650dbc70078","type":"text","x":1380,"y":1570,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**Assessment**\nStrongly supports an attempt at remote SYSTEM-level execution through a new service."},
		{"id":"51b6dbc1ed6a","type":"text","x":1380,"y":1780,"width":340,"height":200,"text":"**Unconfirmed**\nRegistration shows the configured command, not that it ran. How the script reached THM-SREYES is not shown.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"9c1983551dc0","type":"text","x":1840,"y":550,"width":340,"height":140,"text":"## Phase 5\nData staging on THM-SREYES\n`05:54:47-05:56:38`","color":"6"},
		{"id":"66e46882acaa","type":"text","x":1840,"y":740,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**POC 8 - External connection**\n05:54:47 SYSTEM PowerShell (PID 12408) connects to `104.18.32.47:443`","color":"5"},
		{"id":"98085e4dc862","type":"text","x":1840,"y":950,"width":340,"height":220,"text":"**POC 9 - 7-Zip archive**\n05:56:38 `7z.exe a -mx=1 C:\\Windows\\Temp\\nx_build_beta.7z C:\\Dev\\NeuralNexus\\Build\\*`\nParent: hidden PowerShell running `svchost_update.ps1` as SYSTEM","color":"1"},
		{"id":"89588830cc04","type":"text","x":1840,"y":1220,"width":340,"height":140,"text":"**Assessment**\nConsistent with staging NeuralNexus build artifacts for removal."},
		{"id":"66cea0f2f796","type":"text","x":1840,"y":1410,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**Unconfirmed**\n`104.18.32.47` needs separate attribution. Archive contents and successful creation are unverified.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"082fba93abbd","type":"text","x":2300,"y":550,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"## Phase 6\nOutbound connection after archiving\n`05:57:43`","color":"6"},
		{"id":"8c8f080a274d","type":"text","x":2300,"y":760,"width":340,"height":260,"text":"**POC 10 - Network connection (EID 3)**\n05:57:43 SYSTEM PowerShell (PID 14264) connects to `45.147.230.131:8067`\nSame Process GUID as the PowerShell that launched 7-Zip","color":"1"},
		{"id":"36b77b1d45e1","type":"text","x":2300,"y":1070,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**Assessment**\nStrongest link between staging and external activity. Supports suspected exfiltration."},
		{"id":"6327c415a071","type":"text","x":2300,"y":1280,"width":340,"height":160,"text":"**Unconfirmed**\nEvent ID 3 shows a connection, not data contents or volume. Theft is not confirmed.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"18d8f0d78729","type":"text","x":0,"y":2150,"width":320,"height":260,"text":"**Hypothesis A - Word doc started it**\nBasis: Word opened the `.docm` and a hidden PowerShell child decoded a download. How the document triggered it is not proven."},
		{"id":"9629da551df8","type":"text","x":380,"y":2150,"width":320,"height":260,"text":"**Hypothesis B - Script copied to THM-SREYES**\nBasis: the service references `C:\\Windows\\Temp\\svchost_update.ps1` on the target. An SMB copy via `C$` is plausible but not shown."},
		{"id":"50e55f004cfa","type":"text","x":0,"y":2460,"width":320,"height":260,"text":"**Hypothesis C - Aim was exfiltration**\nBasis: 7-Zip archived the build directory, then the same PowerShell process connected to the suspicious IP. Transfer is not proven."},
		{"id":"761b21739660","type":"text","x":380,"y":2480,"width":320,"height":220,"text":"**Hypothesis D - Service gave privileged execution**\nBasis: EID 4697 sets `SvcUpdate` to run PowerShell as LocalSystem, followed by a remote start. Verify with target-side logs."},
		{"id":"266f29e28669","type":"text","x":860,"y":2170,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**Network before execution**\nConnection at 05:42:16 predates Word process creation at 05:43:10.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"fe8698b27460","type":"text","x":1240,"y":2150,"width":320,"height":200,"text":"**Credential-access timestamps**\nVaultCmd data has conflicting renderings around 05:42 and 05:43.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"5f685166f2d2","type":"text","x":860,"y":2400,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**Script-transfer gap**\nNo event shows `C:\\Windows\\Temp\\svchost_update.ps1` being created on THM-SREYES.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"5b0578951395","type":"text","x":1240,"y":2400,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**Connection aggregation**\nTotal count, duration and bytes transferred are not established.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"f2b78f01519b","type":"text","x":860,"y":2610,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**External destination attribution**\n`104.18.32.47:443` is not conclusively linked to the archive.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"b926c49c6312","type":"text","x":1760,"y":2150,"width":320,"height":220,"text":"**Confirmed**\nSuspicious process execution, domain-enumeration commands, remote service registration, archive command, outbound connections","color":"4"},
		{"id":"49409d6e85de","type":"text","x":1760,"y":2390,"width":320,"height":200,"text":"**Not yet confirmed**\nCredential theft, target-side script transfer, successful remote execution, archive contents, successful exfiltration","color":"3"},
		{"id":"5af4607dd932","type":"text","x":2140,"y":2150,"width":320,"height":220,"text":"## Final classification\n**True Positive** - suspected intrusion with lateral movement and potential exfiltration. Keep escalated until open questions are resolved.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"33a6f2307b60","type":"text","x":1000,"y":2940,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**1. Preserve logs**\nSecurity, Sysmon, PowerShell, SMB, firewall and proxy logs from both hosts.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"92911495df4d","type":"text","x":1380,"y":2940,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**2. Trace the logon**\nCorrelate Event ID 4624 with logon ID `0x24F6572` for logon type and source address.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"00150af5620a","type":"text","x":1760,"y":2940,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**3. Verify service execution**\nCheck service install, service state and process creation on THM-SREYES.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"8fe46dddd7af","type":"text","x":2140,"y":2940,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**4. Find the transfer**\nSearch for file creation or transfer of `C:\\Windows\\Temp\\svchost_update.ps1` on the target.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"6721b3abb595","type":"text","x":1000,"y":3170,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**5. Inspect the archive**\nPreserve `nx_build_beta.7z`; establish size, contents, hash and creation status.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"c05c82fb0d9a","type":"text","x":1380,"y":3170,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**6. Review network telemetry**\nCheck `45.147.230.131:8067` and `104.18.32.47:443` for counts and bytes transferred.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"91afaf5762c6","type":"text","x":1760,"y":3170,"width":320,"height":160,"text":"**7. Hunt environment-wide**\nSearch for the script name, archive name, service name and suspicious destinations.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"cc0bac5b6da6","type":"text","x":2140,"y":3150,"width":320,"height":200,"text":"**8. Contain**\nFollowing IR procedure, isolate affected systems and contain compromised accounts. Preserve evidence before cleanup.","color":"2"}
	],
	"edges":[
